# Settings → Automation → Runs replaces Build Analytics (all domains, paginated)

Context: Settings → Automation → Build Analytics showed one domain's build
history behind a domain + version dropdown, with aggregate summary cards on
top — a second, weaker view of what Knowledge Graph → Management → Runs
already does better, and it had no analytics-run history at all. It is
replaced by a cross-domain Runs page: the same two-tab layout as the
per-domain page (Build runs / Analytics runs), a Domain column, a Domain
filter defaulting to "All domains", and real server-side pagination — the
whole registry's history has no natural bound the way one domain's does.
Admin-only, since it exposes every domain. The rendering half of
`domain-runs.js` was extracted into a shared module so the two pages cannot
drift apart. Design:
`documentation/superpowers/specs/2026-08-04-settings-all-domains-runs-design.md`.

Changes:

1. `src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py`
   New `load_all_build_runs()` / `load_all_graph_analytics_runs()` on the
   store abstraction, both keyword-only (`folder`, `limit`, `offset`) and both
   returning `(page_rows, total)` so a caller can render page counts without
   reading every row. Defaults are `([], 0)`, so stores without the tables
   degrade to an empty page. `BuildRunEntry` and `GraphAnalyticsRun` gained an
   optional `domain` key (`total=False`), set only by the cross-domain reads.
2. `src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py`
   Both methods implemented as a `COUNT(*)` plus a
   `ORDER BY … LIMIT %s OFFSET %s` page sharing one predicate string, so the
   quoted total always answers the same question as the page. `d.folder = %s`
   is omitted entirely (not bound to NULL) when no domain is selected, and
   `d.folder AS domain` is mapped onto each row. New `_scalar_total()` reads
   `COUNT(*) AS total` whatever the row factory is.
3. `src/back/objects/registry/RegistryService.py`
   Pass-throughs for both, each swallowing store exceptions into `([], 0)`
   like the per-domain readers around them.
4. `src/back/objects/domain/SettingsService.py`
   `get_all_build_runs_result()` / `get_all_analytics_runs_result()` over a
   shared `_all_runs_result(kind, …)` — the two differ only in which registry
   method they call, so they share one body. Both return the paging envelope
   (`runs`, `total`, `limit`, `offset`, `domain`) and raise `ValidationError`
   when the registry is not configured.
5. `src/api/routers/internal/settings.py`
   `GET /settings/runs/build` and `GET /settings/runs/analytics`, with
   `domain` (empty = every domain), `limit` (1–200, default 25) and
   `offset` (≥ 0). Admin-only by virtue of the `/settings` prefix — neither
   was added to the middleware's read-only exception list. The per-domain
   `GET /settings/build-runs/{domain}` and
   `GET /settings/build-analytics/{domain}` are kept for programmatic use even
   though their UI caller is gone.
6. `src/front/static/global/js/runs-render.js` (new)
   `window.RunsRender`: everything that turns a run into HTML — formatters,
   status/kind badges, scope, the two row-cell builders and the two modal-body
   builders. The row builders take `{domain, handler}` instead of being
   duplicated per page, and the modal builders return HTML rather than writing
   to a hardcoded element id, so each page injects into its own modal.
7. `src/front/static/domain/js/domain-runs.js`
   Rendering removed (~230 lines); it now owns only the two fetches, the
   element ids and the `_runsLoaded` latch, delegating to `RunsRender`. The
   `!data.success` / catch contract and the isolation of the two loaders are
   unchanged.
8. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_runs.html` (new)
   The page: Domain filter, two tabs, per-tab loading / empty / error /
   pagination elements (`sr…` ids so a Runs id is never ambiguous between the
   two pages), and a rows selector (25 / 50 / 100).
9. `src/front/static/config/js/settings-runs.js` (new)
   One descriptor per tab (URL, ids, cell builder) driving a single loader, so
   the two tabs are data rather than two copies. Sequential awaits keep one
   tab's failure from blanking the other's table. Changing the Domain filter
   or the page size resets the offset to 0 — keeping it would land on a page
   that may not exist in the new result set. Reloads on every section entry
   rather than latching once.
10. `src/front/templates/settings.html`
    `runs-section` and the two scripts moved inside the
    `user_role == 'admin'` block; the two run-details modals rendered at page
    level (a modal inside a hidden `.sidebar-section` shows its backdrop but
    leaves the dialog invisible). `build-analytics-section` and
    `build-analytics.js` removed.
11. `src/front/config/menu_config.json`
    Automation → Build Analytics replaced by Runs (`bi-list-check`,
    `admin_only: true`).
12. `src/front/templates/dtwin.html`, `src/front/templates/domain.html`
    Load `runs-render.js` before `domain-runs.js`.
13. `src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_build_analytics.html`,
    `src/front/static/config/js/build-analytics.js`
    Deleted.
14. `src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/schema.sql`
    `build_runs` comment now names the two Runs pages instead of the removed
    Build Analytics panel.
15. `tests/units/registry/test_registry_store.py`
    Contract tests against the in-memory fake (span domains newest-first, rows
    carry their domain, folder scoping, total independent of paging, disjoint
    consecutive pages, offset past the end, unknown domain) plus Lakebase SQL
    tests pinning the conditional `d.folder` predicate, the bound-param order,
    the shared count/page predicate and the count-not-page-length total.
16. `tests/units/settings/test_all_runs_endpoints.py` (new)
    Both endpoints through a real `TestClient`: paging defaults and echo,
    `limit`/`offset` validation, empty domain treated as all domains, unknown
    domain as an empty page not an error, unconfigured registry as a 400.
17. `tests/units/front/test_settings_runs_page.py` (new)
    Rendered-HTML assertions for the section, tabs, per-tab state elements,
    Domain column, filter, pagination controls and both modals; that the
    section and its script are inside the admin block; that the shared module
    loads before each of its three consumers; and that Build Analytics is gone
    from the page, the scripts, the menu and the filesystem.
18. `tests/units/auth/test_permission_middleware.py`
    Regression guard: both new readers stay admin-only for a builder.
19. `tests/units/front/test_runs_page.py`, `tests/units/api/test_ui_rendering.py`
    Retargeted at the moved behaviour: the analytics badge helper and the
    failed-run dashing now live in `runs-render.js`; the Settings page test
    names the Runs section.
20. `documentation/api.md`, `documentation/user-guide.md`,
    `documentation/development.md`
    New "Run History Endpoints" section covering all four readers (including
    the two per-domain ones kept for API use); a cross-reference from the
    per-domain Runs page to the admin all-domains one; UI-test table updated.

Verified live against the running dev app and its Lakebase registry:
`/settings/runs/build` reports `total: 30` with `domain` on every row,
consecutive pages are disjoint, `?domain=contactcenter` narrows to 2,
an unknown domain returns an empty page, and `?limit=201` is rejected 422.

