## Correct distribution bin docstrings after review

Context: Review of `_bin_index_expression` found the docstring describing bare
`CAST(... AS INTEGER)` truncation while the code emits `CAST(ROUND(..., 10) AS
INTEGER)` — the ROUND is load-bearing for binary64 boundary values and was
unexplained. The portability claim overstated Postgres execute support, and the
`bins` floor guard had no comment tying it to divide-by-zero in the general
branch.

Changes:

1. `src/back/core/graph_analysis/JobMetrics.py`
   Align the third docstring bullet with the emitted SQL, document why
   `ROUND(..., 10)` is required, soften the engine guarantee to SQLite +
   Databricks/Spark execute with sqlglot parse-only Postgres, and note the
   zero-bins precondition on `distributions_query`.

