## Ask for the analysis scope at launch instead of parking it in the toolbar

## Context

The Entity Type dropdown sat in the Analytics toolbar but only took effect when
a run started — it had no `onchange` and changing it redrew nothing. That made
it possible for the toolbar to contradict the screen: run across all types,
then pick "Customer" without re-running, and Interpret posted
`class_filter: ["Customer"]` for full-graph data while the subtitle still said
all types. The agent would then describe a scope nobody had computed.

Three consumers read the live select (Interpret's payload, the funnel subtitle,
and the Data Model Health "was filtered" flag), so the dropdown was acting as
the app's record of what was on screen while simultaneously being an editable
control. Moving it into a launch dialog separates those two roles.

## Changes

1. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_analytics.html` — removed the
   Entity Type label and select from the toolbar and added
   `#analyticsScopeModal`, following the `analyticsMetricModal` pattern already
   in the file. The select is *moved*, not duplicated, so `_loadEntityTypes`
   and `_populateTypeSelect` still find it by id. Footer is Cancel plus a
   primary Run Analysis. The toolbar button now calls `analyticsOpenScope()`.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-analytics.js` — added `_resultScope`, the
   class URI the displayed result was computed with, derived from
   `meta.class_filter` (and cleared when absent, so a full-graph re-run stops
   advertising the previous type). Repointed the subtitle, Interpret and Data
   Model Health to it. `_getSelectedTypes()` now has exactly one reader: the
   compute request, which is the scope being *requested*.
3. Same file — `analyticsOpenScope` resets the select to the full graph on
   every open, refuses to open when the job is unavailable, and awaits
   `_loadEntityTypes()` rather than firing it off unawaited as the old fallback
   did, so the dialog cannot appear offering only "All types".
4. Same file — extracted `_typeLabel` so the dropdown option and the subtitle
   share one label format, and `_scopeLabel` to resolve a URI back to that
   label (the subtitle holds a URI now, not the option's text).
5. `tests/units/front/test_analytics_dashboard.py` — added
   `TestScopeIsAskedForAtLaunch` and `TestResultScopeDescribesWhatIsDisplayed`
   (15 tests). Each was verified to fail when the behaviour it pins is
   reverted, including mutations that restore the live-select read in Interpret,
   drop the else-null that clears a stale scope, and put the select back in the
   toolbar.
6. `documentation/user-guide.md`, `documentation/features.md` — rewrote the
   "Running an Analysis" steps and the Graph Analytics summary for the dialog.

Not moved: Top N and Log scale act on what is already rendered, so they stay in
the toolbar rather than a pre-run dialog.

