# Line the Analytics KPI strip up with the tab container

## Context

The KPI tiles overhung the tab strip below them on the right. `.ob-tabs` and
`.ob-tab-content` are inset 12px from the right (components.css, main.css) to
match `.section-header`'s `padding-right`, and the KPI row was a Bootstrap
`.row`, which is not.

Measured in headless Chrome against the real cascade, at 1500 / 1100 / 800 /
500px viewports: left edges already agreed, the right edge was out by 11.9px.

A `.row` cannot be lined up by simply adding the same 12px, because its negative
gutters (`margin-right: -0.25rem` against the columns' `padding-right: 0.25rem`)
shift the tile's edge a further 4px — the compensating value would have been an
unexplainable `-8px`. Dropping to a grid removes that arithmetic and matches the
`.analytics-dist-strip` pattern already used in this stylesheet.

## Changes

1. `src/front/static/query/css/query-analytics.css` — new
   `.analytics-kpi-strip`: a six-track `minmax(0, 1fr)` grid with `gap: 0.5rem`
   (the old `g-2`) and `margin-right: 12px` to match the tab container. Media
   queries at 991.98px and 767.98px reproduce the `col-lg-2` / `col-md-4` /
   `col-6` behaviour, so the tiles still go 6 → 3 → 2 across.
2. `src/front/templates/partials/dtwin/_query_analytics.html` — the stats row
   uses the new class, and the six `col-6 col-md-4 col-lg-2` wrapper divs are
   gone since the grid places the tiles directly. Every `aStat*` id is unchanged,
   so `_renderAnalyticsData` is untouched.
3. `tests/units/front/test_analytics_dashboard.py` — added
   `TestTheKpiStripLinesUpWithTheTabs` (6 tests) pinning the grid, the 12px
   inset, the `minmax(0, 1fr)` tracks, and both breakpoints. One test pairs the
   strip's inset with `.ob-tab-content`'s so the two cannot drift apart. Four
   mutations were run and all caught: dropping the inset, reverting to a bare
   `1fr`, changing a breakpoint's track count, and restoring the Bootstrap row.

## Verification

Re-measured after the change: `RIGHT_DELTA` and `LEFT_DELTA` are 0.0 at 1500 /
1100 / 800 / 500px, and the tiles-per-row count is 6 at ≥992px, 3 at 900px and 2
at 700px and below — the same as the Bootstrap columns produced.

