## Final review fixes for session-file-lifecycle branch

**Context.** Eight findings from the whole-branch code review of `fix/session-file-lifecycle`
were addressed. The changes harden the reaper cutoff against the touch-throttle
interaction, add tests that would have caught each finding, close a second
path-sink in `Mapping.save_mappings_to_session`, introduce a single predicate
(`is_valid_session_id`) as the canonical shape check, and make minor log and
documentation improvements.

1. `src/back/objects/session/FileSessionMiddleware.py` — changed reaper cutoff
   from `now - max_age` to `now - max_age - _SESSION_TOUCH_INTERVAL` so a
   session last used inside the touch-throttle window is never reaped while
   its cookie is still valid; updated the docstring to state the relationship.
   Added `is_valid_session_id(value: str) -> bool` public predicate built on
   `_SESSION_ID_RE` so the shape check has one source of truth.  Used it in
   `_get_session_id_from_cookie` and `reap_expired_sessions` (replacing direct
   `_SESSION_ID_RE.fullmatch` calls).  Changed `entry.stat()` to
   `entry.stat(follow_symlinks=False)` so dangling 32-hex symlinks are aged
   and removed rather than logged at warning level on every boot.  Guarded
   the debug-log block with `if session_data:` so it only fires when there is
   content to describe.
2. `src/back/objects/session/__init__.py` — exported `is_valid_session_id`.
3. `src/back/objects/mapping/Mapping.py` — imported `is_valid_session_id`; added
   a shape-validation guard in `save_mappings_to_session` after the empty-id
   check, logging a warning and returning without touching the filesystem when
   the id is malformed.
4. `tests/units/core/test_middleware_session.py` — re-fixtured
   `test_an_expired_session_file_is_removed`, `test_an_unrelated_old_file_is_left_alone`,
   `test_a_near_miss_name_is_left_alone`, and `test_one_undeletable_file_does_not_stop_the_sweep`
   to use age 100_000 (> the new 90_000 grace window).  Added
   `test_a_session_in_the_grace_window_survives` (the case the old cutoff got
   wrong), `TestLifespanWiresReaper.test_reaper_is_called_at_startup_with_session_settings`
   (patches `reap_expired_sessions` and asserts it is called with the correct
   arguments from the lifespan), `test_traversal_cookie_on_write_creates_no_file_outside_session_dir`
   (end-to-end regression for the arbitrary-file-write exploit),
   `test_a_dangling_symlink_is_reaped_not_warned_forever`, and
   `test_a_directory_named_with_32_hex_chars_survives`.
5. `tests/units/mapping/test_pge_session_extras_retention.py` — updated the
   session_id from `"sess-pge-cap"` to a valid 32-hex id; added
   `test_save_mappings_to_session_rejects_traversal_id`.
6. `documentation/code_organization.md` — rewrote "their mtime tracks last use"
   to "their mtime records last use (refreshed at most hourly)" to reflect the
   throttle.

